 of incumbency, a strong cash position, and endorsements including a major federal employee union. Republican Gerald Malloy, an Army veteran who won his primary in August, has raised only about $58,000 and has no outside support on record.\n\nPolling reinforces the picture: University of New Hampshire surveys from June through September show Balint leading by 30 or more points in head-to-head matchups, and a September market prices her win probability near 98 percent. Analysts have described the race as a cruise for the incumbent. With minimal spending against her and a favorable environment, an upset would require an extraordinary shift in the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9976, "margin": 26.51}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9998, "margin": 33.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 32.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 26.0}]}